{"name":"Quiet Bay","hex":"#6597cc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"quiet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["With little or no sound; free of disturbing noise.","Having little motion or activity; calm."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause (someone or something) to become quiet.","To become quiet or calm."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quiet"},{"term":"bay","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Batuley."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A body of water (especially the sea) contained by a concave shoreline.","A bank or dam to keep back water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay"},{"title":"Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Bay is a hair coat color of horses, characterized by a reddish-brown or brown body color with a black point coloration on the mane, tail, ear edges, and lower legs. Bay is one of the most common coat colors in many horse breeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/BayMare.jpg/330px-BayMare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbn